{
  "id": "pseudoconditioning",
  "term": "pseudoconditioning",
  "definition": "Pseudoconditioning is a behavioral response that can look like a conditioned fear reaction but is generally considered not to reflect actual learning. In this context, it is used as a comparison for fear responses that resemble conditioning in behavior while differing from learned fear at a molecular level.",
